 we had perfectly balanced our  ecology and these guys are bringing  camels they also start growing a ton of  non-native plants  like sugar and when they started growing  sugar there was one  native species in australia that was  very excited  that native species looked like this  gray back beetle who was stoked about  the fact that these british people were  growing sugar cane  so they just started to feast on all  these sugar farms  so now the europeans now independent  australians  instead of being like hey maybe we  shouldn't grow sugar here because  every time we grow it it gets infested  by these beetles  instead they're like let's go to hawaii  and get a bunch of frogs  the idea is that the frogs would eat the  beetles and then the beetles would go  away  right but no the frogs or the cane toads  specifically had no natural predator in  australia so they just  exploded in their numbers and they  became a pest in and of themselves hey  look those frogs are eating all their  crops  okay one more example here that i have  to tell you about before i get back to  the border fence  one more because i can't not talk about  this so  back in 1932 emus these like big giant  weird birds  were harassing the farmers and so the  australian government sent out  the australian army thousands of  rounds of ammunition to fight these emus  and to kill them off  so that they could control the  population the best part about the story  is that the emus  won the war i honestly i need to make a  video  specifically about the emu wars because  it's just too nuts if you want me to do  that let me know because i  want to do that okay so those are all  the ways in which  the european settlers brought invasive  species to this ecologically unique  place  and sort of started to mess with the  balance one of the big  animals that the british brought over  when they were settling australia  were these guys sheep sheep  have wool and meat and were a big deal  in england and so the australia